-- title:
--   Index of ±(Γ∩Γ₀(Lℓ)) for Γ₁(L)≤Γ≤Γ₀(L)
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a natural number with $L \neq 0$, let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ satisfying $\Gamma_1(L) \le \Gamma \le \Gamma_0(L)$, where $\Gamma_0$ and $\Gamma_1$ are the usual congruence subgroups of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\ell$ be a prime number. Write $\pm\Delta$ for the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ generated by a subgroup $\Delta$ together with the integer powers of $-1$, i.e. the join $\Delta \sqcup \langle -1 \rangle$. The assertion is an equality of indices in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$:
--   $$[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \pm(\Gamma \cap \Gamma_0(L\ell))] = [\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \pm\Gamma] \cdot \begin{cases} \ell, & \ell \mid L,\\ \ell+1, & \ell \nmid L,\end{cases}$$
--   the intersection being the meet $\Gamma \sqcap \Gamma_0(L\ell)$ and the case distinction being given by the divisibility $\ell \mid L$. Both sides are natural numbers in the sense of `Subgroup.index`, so the statement also encodes that one index is zero exactly when the other is; in fact both are finite here.
--
--   This is the standard index computation for adding $\ell$ to the level of a group between $\Gamma_1(L)$ and $\Gamma_0(L)$, in the form needed for groups containing $-1$: the relative index is $\ell+1$ (the points of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_\ell)$) when $\ell \nmid L$ and $\ell$ when $\ell \mid L$. It is used in the rank computation [`ModularCurve.finrankAlong_heckeBetaModLH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrankAlong_heckeBetaModLH) for spaces of modular forms at level $L\ell$, and rests on the relative index computations for $\Gamma_0(N\ell)$ in $\Gamma_0(N)$ and for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(M\ell)$ in $\Gamma_1(M)$, together with surjectivity of reduction $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \to \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/N)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CongruenceSubgroup_index_inf_gamma0_mul_sup_zpowers_neg_one_of_gamma1_le_of_le_gamma0.lean

